The Memory of a Descending King.

Hamlet, the examiner.
Romeo, the counter and keeper of a stack.

Act I: The remembered count.
Scene I: A beginning.

[Enter Hamlet and Romeo]

Hamlet:
 You are as good as the sum of a fair flower and a flower.

Scene II: Descending.

Hamlet:
 Remember yourself.
 Open your heart!
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a flower.
 Are you better than nothing?
 If so, let us return to Scene II.

Scene III: Memory reverses the count.

Hamlet:
 Recall your past.
 Open your heart!
 Recall your past.
 Open your heart!
 Recall your past.
 Open your heart!
 You are as good as the sum of a fair fair fair flower and a fair flower.
 Speak your mind!

[Exeunt]
